  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Why compile, not retrieve",
      "items": [
        "RAG searches the sources again on every question, so nothing learned on one question helps the next. Here every source is read once, in full, and folded into pages that already exist, with links and a provenance trail.",
        "The payoff compounds: the tenth source lands into a wiki that already knows the first nine. The cost is that compilation is judgment work, so ingest keeps you in the session."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Three layers, who writes where",
      "items": [
        "raw/ is yours and immutable: the agent reads it and never edits or deletes it.",
        "wiki/ is the agent's: pages, index.md, append-only log.md. You read it and rarely touch it; a hand edit is committed separately as yours before the agent works.",
        "The schema is co-owned: AGENTS.md says how the wiki is structured and which workflow runs when; kb.toml holds per-instance data so the tooling stays byte-identical across instances."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "The write path",
      "items": [
        "Capture skills land dated files with provenance frontmatter in raw/ and stop; staging/ingest.md queues what is not yet ingested, with a watch-out per source.",
        "Ingest is one source per session: read in full, discuss takeaways, create or update every page the source touches, add each new page to index.md, append an ingest entry to log.md.",
        "Contestable assertions go in [!claim] callouts with a confidence, a status and an evidence line, so a later source can contest or supersede them in place."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "The read path",
      "items": [
        "A question starts at index.md, one line per page, so the agent routes to the few pages that matter before opening any. Answers come back in conversation with wikilink citations; a synthesis page is filed only when you ask.",
        "Software built on the KB reads it the same way through mcp/server.py: search_kb, read_page, get_index. Writes stay interactive by design (ADR-004)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Keeping it honest",
      "items": [
        "scripts/lint.py is the deterministic half: every page indexed once, every wikilink resolving, every raw: path existing, every claim callout well-formed with a status from kb.toml, orphans and recurring unpaged terms flagged.",
        "The judgment pass is what the script cannot do: contradictions between pages, claims a newer source supersedes, inference stated as fact, missing cross-references.",
        "A schema implication found during ingest is logged, not acted on; it becomes a proposed ADR under decisions/, and an accepted one changes AGENTS.md or the tooling on a branch with review. The schema then disciplines the next run."
      ]
    }
  ]
